_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":3,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":33.3,"_gate_spread":-0.021113562782676606,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":1.384795571728888,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.5535369342661948,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.1342799151871399,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.030866599295015184,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":19.1,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.05874467824893657,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":76.4,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.004290911286247812,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":55.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.003853082465972778,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":93.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.00205,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.4,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Dow Inc., through its subsidiaries, provides various materials science solutions for packaging, infrastructure, mobility, and consumer applications in the United States, Canada, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, India, the Asia Pacific, and Latin America. The company operates through Packaging & Specialty Plastics, Industrial Intermediates & Infrastructure, and Performance Materials & Coatings segments. The Packaging & Specialty Plastics segment provides ethylene, propylene, polyethylene, and aromatics products; and other ethylene derivatives, such as polyolefin elastomers, ethylene vinyl acetate, and ethylene propylene diene monomer rubber. The Industrial Intermediates & Infrastructure segment offers polyurethanes, including propylene oxide, propylene glycol, and polyether polyols; aromatic isocyanates and fully formulated polyurethane systems; and chlor-alkali and vinyl comprising chlorine and caustic soda, ethylene dichloride, and vinyl chloride monomer; and construction chemicals consisting of cellulose ethers, redispersible latex powders, and acrylic emulsions, as well as coatings, adhesives, sealants, elastomers, and composites. The Performance Materials & Coatings segment provides architectural paints and coatings, and industrial coatings; and acrylics-based building blocks, silicon metals, siloxanes, and intermediates. The company also engages in the property and casualty insurance, as well as reinsurance business. The company was founded in 1897 and is headquartered in Midland, Michigan.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Karen S. Carter | CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 31K people. Revenue per employee of $1.3M ranks in the top quartile among Basic Materials peers. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Dow Inc. is a large-cap basic materials business with a $23.9B market cap on $40.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -11% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 14% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $1.4B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 11.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -1.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 700% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Operating margins 13% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 68/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Basic Materials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Basic Materials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 18% margin of safety against estimated fair value"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Dow (DOW) Executive Chairman Made A $25 Million Cancer Care Gift","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/dow-dow-executive-chairman-made-121348936.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794572028.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Downer EDI (ASX:DOW) Shares in Focus: Why Is the ASX 200 Stock on the Radar?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/industrial/downer-edi-asxdow-shares-in-focus-why-is-the-asx-200-stock-on-the-radar","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794563100.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.077,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Downer EDI (ASX:DOW) Shares in Focus: Why Is the ASX 200 Stock Drawing Attention?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/industrial/downer-edi-asxdow-shares-in-focus-why-is-the-asx-200-stock-drawing-attention","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794562980.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.743,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why Is Dow (DOW) Backing U.S. Tariffs Right Now?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nyse-dow/dow/news/why-is-dow-dow-backing-us-tariffs-right-now","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794554293.308,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.44,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["regulatory"]},{"title":"Downer (ASX:DOW) Shares in Focus: Why Is the ASX 200 Stock Drawing Attention?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/value/downer-asxdow-shares-in-focus-why-is-the-asx-200-stock-drawing-attention","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794547860.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Dow Inc. (DOW) is a Top-Ranked Value Stock: Should You Buy?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stoc